DTSTART:20260721T170000Z
DTEND:20260721T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260721T000000Z
SUMMARY:Apocalypse Club
DESCRIPTION:In this immersive workshop series\, teen and young adult 
 writers will journey through a rotating set of potential apocalypses—each 
 one revealing new challenges and unexpected questions about humanity. Every 
 session introduces a different end‑of‑the‑world scenario\, from AI 
 takeovers and climate catastrophes to silence laws\, memory‑loss 
 epidemics\, collapsing societies\, and even the downfall of social media. 
 Through discussion and creative exploration\, writers confront survival 
 strategies\, moral dilemmas\, shifting identities\, and the ways fear and 
 uncertainty reshape human behavior. It’s a chance to think big\, get 
 curious\, and imagine who you might become when the world turns upside 
 down.\n\nPlease contact Dominique at fdiggs@dconc.gov with any questions or 
 concerns.\n\nRecommended for those aged 12-22.  Registration is required.\n
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Dominique Diggs":MAILTO:fdiggs@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Summer Reading, Writing
UID:LibCal-14288-16938824
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16938824
END:VEVENT
