BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260721T213000Z
DTEND:20260721T223000Z
DTSTAMP:20260721T000000Z
SUMMARY:Unearthing The Stories We Tell Ourselves: Imposter Syndrome and Self-Trust
DESCRIPTION:Most people have heard of imposter syndrome or imposter 
 phenomenon: the feeling that your work isn't as good as others think\, that 
 someone is about to find out\, that success so far has mostly been luck. It 
 is a very common human experience. This session digs into where that inner 
 narrator comes from\, why it tends to get louder during hard seasons of 
 health\, stress\, or major change\, and how writing can help people find a 
 more grounded and honest story underneath it. Participants often leave 
 surprised by how long that quieter\, truer voice has been there\, waiting 
 to be unearthed.
LOCATION:Meeting Room #4347\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Alexandra Wurst":MAILTO:awurst@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development, Community Engagement, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16912351
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16912351
END:VEVENT
