SUMMARY:Unearth a Story: Telling Your Family Story
DESCRIPTION:Every family has stories waiting to be discovered! Join us for 
 an intergenerational program where kids\, parents\, grandparents\, and 
 caregivers explore the stories that shape our lives and communities. 
 \n\nDrop in and explore a variety of interactive stations designed to spark 
 conversation and creativity. Families can use conversation prompts to 
 interview one another\, examine historical photographs and archival 
 materials from Durham families of the past\, create maps of their homes or 
 neighborhoods\, and write stories inspired by what they discover. 
 \n\nThrough memories\, maps\, and imagination\, participants will 
 “unearth” the stories that connect generations and bring our 
 community’s history to life.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Christina Economou":MAILTO:ceconomou@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:North Carolina Collection, Summer Reading
