BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260725T180000Z
DTEND:20260725T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260725T000000Z
SUMMARY:Durham Grown: The Durham County Library Garden Club
DESCRIPTION:Exploring Summer Light in the Garden! \n\nJoin Jeanine Brandi 
 of J. Bee Studios to learn how to make the most of these long\, light 
 filled summer days! Learn how to take beautiful photographs that capture 
 your garden and all of its abundance! You will learn to use whatever 
 equipment you have to document your garden or other places that inspire 
 you. Jeanine will present photographs from different gardens she has 
 documented through the years as examples. You will learn practical ways to 
 improve your photo skills to savor the seasons and capture these moments 
 before they pass! \n\nJeanine Brandi is the founder of J.Bee Studios- 
 specializing in landscape design\, photography\, and flowers. She has a 
 Bachelor of Science in Photography from Syracuse University and worked in 
 the photography field for many years before returning to school for 
 Landscape Architecture. She received a master's degree in Landscape 
 Architecture from Rhode Island School of Design. She enjoys creating and 
 documenting landscapes to live in\, focused on interaction\, sustainability 
 and stewardship. \n \n\nConnect with Jeanine on Instagram @j.bee.studios or 
 on the web at J. Bee Studios or JBrandi\n\n\n\nSaturday July 25th starting 
 at 2 pm in the auditorium at the Durham County Main Library located at 300 
 North Roxboro Street.  \n\n\n\nParking is available in the library lot or 
 at the North Queen Street Garage which is locate at 115 North Queen Street 
 which is located directly across the street from the library. Parking is 
 free in the garage. Bring your parking ticket to a library service point 
 for validation.     \n\n\n\nImage description: A soft pink almond blossom 
 taken at Fat Uncle Farms in Winter 2012 \n\nPhoto credit Jeanine Brandi\, 
 J. Bee Studios
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Classes & Lectures, Durham, Environmental, Gardening, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-15882796
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15882796
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
