SUMMARY:Picnic in the Park
DESCRIPTION:Join us outdoors for a relaxed Picnic in the Park. Enjoy a 
 casual\, open discussion of ROGUE by Julie Kagawa\, surrounded by fresh air 
 and green space. Participants are welcome to bring their own snacks and 
 drinks to enjoy during the meetup. This laid-back gathering is a great way 
 to connect with other readers\, share book recommendations\, and unwind in 
 a peaceful setting. All teens are welcome\; no registration 
 required.\n\nThis month we will meet at Duke Park\n\n106 W. Knox Street\; 
 Durham\, NC 27701\n\nIn case of rain\, we will meet at North Regional 
 Library.  Please contact Ms. Dom at fdiggs@dconc.gov with any questions or 
 accessibility concerns.\n\nAbout ROGUE: \n\nEmber Hill left the dragon 
 organization Talon to take her chances with rebel dragon Riley and his crew 
 of rogues. But she can't forget Garret\, the soldier of the dragonslaying 
 Order of St. George who saved her from a Talon assassin--and by doing so\, 
 signed his own death warrant.\nDetermined to save Garret from execution\, 
 Ember must convince Riley to help her break into the Order's headquarters. 
 With assassins after them and Ember's own twin brother helping Talon hunt 
 her down\, the rogues find an unexpected ally in Garret and a new 
 perspective on the underground battle between Talon and St. George. Soon 
 Ember must decide: should she retreat to fight another day...or start an 
 all-out war?.\n\nThis book is available in the following formats: physical 
 copy\, Hoopla ebook\, and Hoopla audiobook.
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Dominique Diggs":MAILTO:fdiggs@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-16726920
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16726920
END:VEVENT
