BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260728T220000Z
DTEND:20260728T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260728T000000Z
SUMMARY:DRAGONFLIES!
DESCRIPTION:DRAGONFLIES! \n\nWho? What? Where? When? Why? \n\n 
 \n\n\n\nUsing motion camouflage to attack prey and rivals... \n\nGiant 
 multifaceted compound eyes that can see in 360 degrees... \n\nPredators in 
 all life stages...consuming prey as large as tadpoles and small fish... 
 \n\nGigantic prehistoric distant relatives had wingspans of up to 30 
 inches... \n\nFlying at speeds of up to 18 miles per hour in six different 
 directions and four types of flight... \n\n \n\n\n\nWho are these insects 
 that were among the first to evolve and exist with and before dinosaurs? 
 What kind of prey do they eat? Where do dragonflies live? When do female 
 dragonflies feign death? Why are dragonflies iridescent?  \n\n \n\n\n\nJoin 
 Chris Goforth\, head of Collaborative Science at the North Carolina Museum 
 of Natural Science\, to learn more about these masters of flight!  \n\n\n\n 
 \n\nChris Goforth is the head of Collaborative Science at the North 
 Carolina Museum of Natural Science and spends her day connecting visitors 
 to scientific research they can take part in as non-experts.  She holds a 
 bachelor's degree in biology and a master’s degree in entomology and has 
 published studies on dragonflies and giant water bugs.  She was scared of 
 insects as a young child\, but dragonflies have been her favorite insects 
 as long as she’s liked bugs.  She is most interested in their fascinating 
 behaviors. \n\n \n\n\n\nTuesday July 28th starting at 6 p.m. in the Durham 
 County Main Library auditorium located at 300 North Roxboro Street in 
 Durham.      \n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the 
 North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind 
 the apartments directly across the street from the library. Parking at the 
 garage is free. Please bring your parking ticket to a service point for 
 validation.        \n\n \n\nRegistration is appreciated to receive an email 
 reminder\, cancellation link\, and program updates. Seating is first come 
 first served. Registration does not hold or guarantee a seat.      
 \n\nThere will be no live animals or insects at this event.    \n\n 
 \n\nQuestions? Email mkoslofsky@dconc.gov \n\n \n\nImage description: 
 Skimmer Slaty\, Libellula incesta\, a large dusky dark blue dragonfly found 
 statewide. \n\nPhoto credit: Alan Schmierer
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-15493391
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15493391
END:VEVENT
