BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260729T133000Z
DTEND:20260729T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T000000Z
SUMMARY:Day 3 – Climate-Smart Agriculture\, Assistive Technologies & Digital Technologies
DESCRIPTION:Free NC A&T & PHIRST® workshop series. Attend 1 day\, multiple 
 days\, or all 4: business\, agriculture\, technology & future 
 farming.\n\nPHIRST® PovertyZero™ Farms & Food Workshop Series with NC 
 A&T\n\nJoin North Carolina A&T State University and PHIRST® for a free 
 four-day workshop series focused on certification pathways\, sustainable 
 agriculture\, practical skills\, enterprise development\, and applied 
 learning. Participants may attend one day\, multiple days\, or the full 
 four-day series.\n\nThe workshop series is designed for farmers\, future 
 farmers\, backyard growers\, entrepreneurs\, educators\, students\, and 
 community leaders seeking practical knowledge\, certification 
 opportunities\, hands-on experience\, and sustainable enterprise 
 strategies.\n\nDAY 3 – CLIMATE-SMART AGRICULTURE\, ASSISTIVE TECHNOLOGIES 
 & DIGITAL TECHNOLOGIES\nParticipants explore climate-smart agricultural 
 practices\, bioenergy production\, cover cropping\, waste-to-resource 
 strategies\, carbon sequestration\, renewable energy\, conservation 
 practices\, assistive technologies\, disability resources\, digital 
 technologies\, and computer applications that improve agricultural 
 productivity and enterprise management.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL GAIN\n Practical 
 agricultural knowledge and skills\n Sustainable farming and enterprise 
 strategies\n Certification opportunities through NC A&T OPPE pathways\n 
 Exposure to innovative technologies and systems\n Networking with 
 agricultural professionals\, educators\, entrepreneurs\, and community 
 leaders\n Real-world examples of scalable agricultural 
 enterprises\n\nAttendance is free\, but registration is required.\nSeating 
 is limited to 150 participants per day. \n\nParking is available in the 
 library parking lot or at the North Queen Street Garage located at 115 
 North Queen Street which is behind the apartments directly across the 
 street from the library. Parking at the garage is free. Please bring your 
 parking ticket to a service point for validation.       \n\nAttend one 
 day\, multiple days\, or the entire four-day series.\n\nLearn. Grow. 
 Innovate. Build Sustainably.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Main Library":MAILTO:main@durhamcountylibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17184404
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17184404
END:VEVENT
