SUMMARY:SKULLS: A Skull Identification with Duke Lemur Center Museum of Natural History
DESCRIPTION:How do fossil hunters identify an animal from just a fragment 
 of skull or a tooth? What can the bones of a skull tell us about how an 
 animal lived? Join paleontologists from the Duke Lemur Center Museum of 
 Natural History to learn how to identify a variety of animals based on 
 their skulls and test your skills with a variety of osteology and fossil 
 specimens!\n\nThis program is a drop-in program\, drop by anytime between 
 11am and 1pm to the Innovation Lab on third floor of Main Library (300 N. 
 Roxboro St.\, Durham\, NC 27701). This program is geared towards ages 8 and 
 up\, all ages welcome. (Ages 10 and under must be accompanied by an 
 adult.)\n\nNote: If you have any accessibility questions or accommodation 
 needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all 
 requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to ensure we 
 can provide the best accommodations possible!\n\n
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
