SUMMARY:STEAM Storytime   Activity at Daughters Coffee and Books
DESCRIPTION:Join the Maker   STEAM team on Tuesday\, August 4th from 
 10:30am-11:15am at Daughters Coffee and Books for a STEAM-related storytime 
 plus hands-on activity! We will read a story about exploring making things 
 and then an activity with 3D printed construction sticks to build your own 
 creation. \n\nThis program is offsite. It is held on Tuesday\, August 4th 
 from 10:30am-11:15am at Daughters Coffee and Books\, located at 5410 NC-55 
 AF\, Durham\, NC 27713. Parking in the shopping center parking lot is free. 
 Registration is required\, and please register each person (adult and 
 child) in attendance as materials and space are limited. The story and 
 activity will be geared towards ages 3-8\; siblings welcome. Adults must 
 remain with their children.\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 2 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible.
