SUMMARY:Maker   STEAM Take and Make: Ready to TTRPG? kit
DESCRIPTION:Ready to create\, act\, and debate through fictional content in 
 a tabletop roleplaying game? This month's Maker   STEAM Take and Make 
 introduces people new to TTRPGs (tabletop roleplaying games) with a few 
 resources to get you started! This kit includes a laser cut dice tower you 
 can put together\, a few acrylic paints and a paintbrush\, and several 
 resources and short one-page scenarios for you to test out your roleplaying 
 skills solo or with a group. (Some materials included are for teens and 
 adults\, specifically.)\n\nKits are located in the shelving unit outside of 
 the Innovation Lab on the Third Floor at Main Library for you to take home 
 and complete.\n\nFirst come\, first serve while supplies last.\n
LOCATION:Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Maker, STEAM
