SUMMARY:Teen Art Club @ South Regional Library
DESCRIPTION:For creatives in grades 6-12:\n\nJoin us for casual creativity 
 sessions with other artists at the South Regional Library! Meetings will 
 have an easy-to-learn art project planned (and coloring sheets at the 
 ready)\, but feel free to bring your sketchbook or current creative 
 project! You also have the option to do an art project of your own choosing 
 instead\, with the materials from our Teen Art Cart: put together a 
 collage\, fold origami\, make a zine...there's all sorts of possibilities! 
 \n\nThe Teen Art Club meets on the first and third Wednesdays of each month 
 in the Children's Programming Room\, to the left of the Teen Space 
 😄\n\nRegistration not required but appreciated!\n\nFeel free to reach 
 out to Ezra\, Senior Teen Librarian and club facilitator\, with any 
 questions at eletson@dconc.gov.\n\n \n
LOCATION:South Regional - Children's Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ezra L.":MAILTO:eletson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Social
