SUMMARY:Cretaceous Crawl: An Extinction-Level Downtown Event 
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading is almost over but don't let your connection 
 with the library go extinct! Some of our librarians are spread around 
 town--find them  to make buttons\, decorate journals\, test your trivia\, 
 find fossils and more in a summer reading finale designed especially for 
 adults. Registration is not required but helps us plan. The route is 
 walkable at three-quarters of a mile in length\, with parking available 
 throughout downtown. Be sure to stop at the CCB Plaza at the end of your 
 adventure to grab a completion prize and to enter a raffle for one of two 
 $50 Spendabull cards!\n\nYou can start your adventure at any of the 
 locations! You can find us at:\n\nQueeny's: 321 E Chapel Hill St Ste 
 100\n\nMontwood Cafe: 123 Market St\, Suite A\n\nThe Parlour: 117 Market 
 St\n\nMuseum of Durham History: 500 W Main St\n\nCCB Plaza: corner of 
 Corcoran and Parrish\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Killion":MAILTO:nkillion@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Friends of the Durham Library, Other, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-16434479
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16434479
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260809T133000Z
DTEND:20260809T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260809T000000Z
SUMMARY:Roaming Readers: A Walking Audiobook Club!
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we walk the trails of RTP while listening to 
 audiobooks! After\, feel free to join us at Drift Coffee Shop & Kitchen RTP 
 for an optional discussion about the book and a chance to meet new 
 people.\n\n \n\nThis month’s suggested audiobook is The Indigo Girl by 
 Natasha Boyd (available on Hoopla). If you have already read it\, or would 
 prefer another title\, we suggest: The Librarian Spy by Madeline Martin 
 (available on Hoopla) or The Saints of Swallow Hill by Donna Everhart 
 (available on Hoopla). \n\n \n\nThis event is for book lovers\, the 
 book-curious\, people who haven’t been able to make time to read (or 
 listen) for fun\, introverts\, extroverts\, exercisers\, caregivers pushing 
 strollers\, (leashed) dog owners\, groups\, singles\, nature lovers\, and 
 multi-taskers!\n\n \n\nAll paces welcome\, please take breaks when you need 
 them. We know it is easy to get transported to another world when listening 
 to your book. Be sure to stay alert as we will be crossing roads and may 
 encounter uneven pavement. \n\n \n\nWhile attendance is free\, please 
 register here to receive reminders and stay in the know for any updates. 
 Free public parking is located on the deck just across the street at 3150 
 Elion Drive. We will meet at 3151 Elion Drive Durham\, NC 27713.\n\n 
 \n\nQuestions? Email Elle at kfarmer@dconc.gov.\n\n \n\nUpcoming 
 dates:\n\nSeptember 13th
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Elle F.":MAILTO:kfarmer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Health & Fitness, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16608359
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16608359
END:VEVENT
