SUMMARY:Miniature Shrines and Shadowboxes!
DESCRIPTION:Miniature Shrines and Shadowboxes! \n\nCelebrate the end of 
 summer and the beginning of the harvest season with all things bountiful 
 and abundant!  Create a mini shrine or shadowbox to honor whatever is 
 bountiful and abundant in your life!  \n\n \nLook through your craft stash 
 or take a trip to the Scrap Exchange and look for small objects and 
 miniature items that call to you (figurines\, shiny rocks or shells\, silk 
 or paper flowers\, baubles\, gears\, beads\, little altars\, quotes or 
 poems\, etc.). We'll have a wide variety of interesting small boxes\, as 
 well as hot glue\, scissors\, decorative elements and paints! \n\nMonday 
 August 10th starting at 5:30 in the Main Library MakerLab located on the 
 first floor. \n\n \n\nRegistration required due to limited supplies. Please 
 cancel your registration if you are unable to attend. Please register each 
 person individually.\n\n All ages welcome\; however\, juveniles of all ages 
 must have an adult guardian with them during the program. \n\n \n\nFor more 
 information email Megan at mkoslofsky@dconc.gov.\n\nPhoto description: An 
 Altoid tin repurposed to make a miniature bookcase
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Durham, Social
