BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260812T170000Z
DTEND:20260812T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260812T000000Z
SUMMARY:Daytime Book Club: My Friends
DESCRIPTION:Come join the Daytime Book Club as we discuss this month's 
 book! New members are always welcome (we love meeting new people!). 
 Registration is appreciated but not required.\n\nThis month we will discuss 
 My Friends by Fredrik Backman. The description for the book is 
 below:\n"Most people don't even notice them: three tiny figures sitting at 
 the end of a long pier in the corner of one of the most famous paintings in 
 the world. Most people think it's just a depiction of the sea. But Louisa\, 
 an artist herself\, knows otherwise and she is determined to find out the 
 story of these three enigmatic figures.\n\nTwenty-five years earlier\, in a 
 distant town\, a group of teenagers find refuge from their difficult home 
 lives by spending their days laughing and telling stories out on a pier. 
 There's Joar\, who never backs down from a fight\; quiet and bookish Ted 
 who is mourning his father\; Ali\, the daughter of a man who never stays in 
 one place for long\; and finally\, there's the artist\, a boy who hoards 
 sleeping pills and shuns attention\, but who possesses an extraordinary 
 gift that might be his ticket to a better life. These four lost souls find 
 in each other a reason to get up each morning\, a reason to dream.\n\nOut 
 of that summer emerges a transcendent work of art\, a painting that will 
 unexpectedly be put into eighteen-year-old Louisa's care. As she struggles 
 to decide what to do with this bequest\, she embarks on a surprise-filled 
 cross-country journey to learn the story of how the painting came to be. 
 The closer she gets to the painting's birthplace\, the more she feels 
 compelled to unleash her own artistic spirit\, but happy endings don't 
 always take the form we expect in this fresh testament to the 
 transformative power of friendship and art."\n\nWe look forward to seeing 
 you all soon!\n\n\nInterested in attending a future Daytime Book Club 
 meeting? Take a look at our reading list below:\n\nMay 2026: To the 
 Lighthouse by Virginia Woolf\n\nJune 2026: The Night Watchman by Louise 
 Erdrich\n\nJuly 2026: A Marriage at Sea by Sophie Elmhirst\n\nAugust 2026: 
 My Friends by Fredrik Backman\n\nSeptember 2026: Wild Dark Shore by 
 Charlotte McConaghy\n\nOctober 2026: The House on Mango Street by Sandra 
 Cisneros\n\nNovember 2026: Midnight in the Garden of Good and Evil by John 
 Berendt\n\nDecember 2026: Orbital by Samantha Harvey\n\nJanuary 2027: What 
 We Can Know by Ian McEwan\n\nFebruary 2027: Song of Solomon by Toni 
 Morrison\n\nMarch 2027: Proud Shoes by Pauli Murray\n\nApril 2027: Isola by 
 Allegra Goodman
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-16576130
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16576130
END:VEVENT
