BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260817T213000Z
DTEND:20260817T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260817T000000Z
SUMMARY:Community Presentation Introducing & Exploring the Recommended Cultural Plan
DESCRIPTION:Durham’s Cultural Roadmap Is Almost Final. Come See What’s 
 In It.\n\nIn the coming months\, City Council and County Commissioners will 
 vote on Durham’s Cultural Roadmap\, a plan shaped by years of resident 
 input that will guide investment in arts and culture for the next 
 decade.\n\nBefore that vote happens\, come see what’s in the plan. 
 \n\nJoin us for a community presentation of the draft plan: the vision\, 
 the four pillars\, and the 10 recommendations that came out of the 
 engagement process. We’ll cover how your input shaped the plan\, what 
 adoption actually involves\, and where you can weigh in on the plan’s 
 implementation.\n\nSeats are limited. Registration is recommended on 
 Eventbrite 
 https://www.eventbrite.com/e/community-presentation-durham-cultural-roadmap-tickets-1995718790626?aff=oddtdtcreator\n\nParking 
 is available in the library parking lot or at the North Queen Street Garage 
 located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind the apartments directly 
 across the street from the library. Parking at the garage is free. Please 
 bring your parking ticket to a service point for validation.      \n\nWant 
 the backstory? Read more at CreativeDurham.org.
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Claudia Aleman":MAILTO:caleman@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Community Engagement, Durham
UID:LibCal-14288-17315359
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17315359
END:VEVENT
