SUMMARY:Heartfulness Meditation
DESCRIPTION:Heartfulness meditation practice is a simple and effective way 
 to integrate meditation into our daily lives. The Heartfulness technique 
 shows us how to gently turn our attention toward our hearts and experience 
 that inner presence for ourselves. There will be a brief introduction and 
 instruction\, followed by a guided relaxation\, leading into a silent 
 heart-centered meditation. Sessions are conducted by a certified 
 Heartfulness meditation instructor and open to everyone over the age of 15. 
 No prior experience necessary. Registration is not required.\n\nIf you have 
 questions about accessibility\, program stimulation levels\, and/or need 
 disability accommodations\, please contact us at 919-560-8593.
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Carmen Ruth":MAILTO:cruth@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Health & Fitness, Low Sensory Stimulation
UID:LibCal-14288-16848862
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16848862
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260817T220000Z
DTEND:20260817T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260817T000000Z
SUMMARY:Adult Story Time -- O. Henry Prize Stories
DESCRIPTION:Read-alouds are for grown-ups too! Join us for a weekday 
 evening adult story time at the North Regional Library. Flop on the carpet 
 with a floor pillow\, pull up a chair\, or sit at a table if you want to 
 bring your own dinner or snacks. Spend an hour listening to read-alouds 
 from books and stories in the library collection. Tea\, coffee\, and hot 
 chocolate will be provided.\n\nThis month: stories from the O. Henry Prize 
 collection. We'll read a few stories from the annual anthology celebrating 
 the best short fiction published in the U.S. and Canada\, a collection 
 well-known for strong narrative voice and compelling 
 plotting.\n\nRegistration is appreciated but not required.\n\nE-mail Bob 
 with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-17092599
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17092599
END:VEVENT
